  "id": "Wandsworth-2026_0924",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "The proposal seeks full planning permission for the erection of a self-contained studio dwelling accessed from Rackham Mews. The dwelling is arranged over a single storey above ground with additional lower-ground accommodation. The development includes a sedum green roof, associated private amenity space in the form of a sunken courtyard garden, and high-quality external materials.\nThere is no change of use associated with the proposal, which introduces a new residential unit (Use Class C3) on a discreet rear-land site.\n",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed dwelling, by reason of its scale and location within part of an undeveloped residential garden would be an inappropriate form of development. The proposed building would be an incongruous feature that would fail to physically integrate with its surroundings and would detract from the local spatial character. As such the proposal would be contrary to policies LP1 and LP7 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and D3(1) of the London Plan (2021).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development would fail to provide the required minimum standard of gross internal area (GIA). The proposed dwelling would therefore provide a substandard level of accommodation for future occupiers and would be contrary to Policy LP27 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).",
    "Reason : 3 - In the absence of sufficient information to demonstrate how the proposal would achieve a minimum on-site carbon emissions reduction of 35%, the proposal fails to demonstrate compliance with Policy LP10 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).\r\n",
    "Reason : 4 - Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate how the proposal would achieve Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG). The applicant must submit a full BNG Metric to demonstrate if any existing lawn is being lost. In addition, additional information regarding tree and protected species, design enhancement measures and construction and mitigation measures would be required. The proposal therefore fails to demonstrate compliance with Policy LP55 Biodiversity of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).\r\n",
    "Reason : 5 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan consisting of the Core Strategy, Development Management Policies Document, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
